{"total_results":5,"perpage":100,"status":1,"results":[{"id":5972294,"title":"Exhibition: A Life Composed: Chin Whai\u0027s Journey Through Music, Literature \u0026 Charity","description":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan data-teams=\u0022true\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan data-teams=\u0022true\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: inherit;\u0022\u003EBorn Tan Leng Gek (\u9648\u9f99\u7389) (1938 \u0026ndash; ), Chin Whai (\u79e6\u6dee) rose to prominence in the 1970s, when his songs captured the hearts of audiences across Singapore, Hong Kong and Southeast Asia. Known for his distinctive vocal style and deeply expressive ballads, he became affectionately known as the \u0026ldquo;King of Ballads\u0026rdquo;.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan data-teams=\u0022true\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: inherit;\u0022\u003EYet, long before he took to the stage as a singer, Chin Whai began his career as a writer, with works appearing in publications such as \u003Ci\u003ESin Chew Daily\u003C/i\u003E\u0026nbsp;and\u0026nbsp;\u003Ci\u003ENanyang Siang Pau\u003C/i\u003E. He published his first book at the age of 22 and went on to produce 11 volumes of poetry, prose and essays. A prolific and versatile creative, he also explored the visual arts as a painter and illustrator.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan data-teams=\u0022true\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: inherit;\u0022\u003EAfter stepping away from the spotlight, Chin Whai devoted himself to giving back to society. Over the years, he headlined numerous charity events, using his music to raise funds and support those in need. His enduring commitment to philanthropy earned him another affectionate title\u0026mdash;the \u0026ldquo;Charity King of Songs\u0026rdquo;.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan data-teams=\u0022true\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: inherit;\u0022\u003EPart of NUS Libraries Chinese Popular Culture Collection series, this exhibition celebrates the the multifaceted creative life and enduring legacy of Chin Whai through a selection of materials from his private papers, generously donated to NUS Libraries. Bringing together his writings, artwork, photographs and other personal materials, the exhibition offers a glimpse into the many facets of an artist whose creative journey has spanned music, literature and the visual arts.\u0026nbsp;\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E","fromTime":"9:00am Thursday, October 8, 2026","toTime":"9:00pm Saturday, October 31, 2026","more_info":"","shortdesc":"\n\nBorn Tan Leng Gek (\u9648\u9f99\u7389) (1938 \u2013 ), Chin Whai (\u79e6\u6dee) rose to prominence in the 1970s, when his songs captured the hearts of audiences across Singapore, Hong Kong and Southeast Asia. Known for his...","shortdesc_was_truncated":true,"registration_cost":"","start":"9:00am","end":"9:00pm","all_day":false,"startdt":"2026-10-08 09:00:00","enddt":"2026-10-31 21:00:00","date":"Thursday, October 8, 2026","ymd":"20261008","year":"2026","monthnum":10,"day":"8","daypostfix":"th","dayfull":"Thursday","dayshort":"Thu","monthfull":"October","monthshort":"Oct","multi_day_event":true,"multi_day_end":{"year":"2026","monthnum":10,"day":"31","daypostfix":"st","dayfull":"Saturday","dayshort":"Sat","monthfull":"October","monthshort":"Oct"},"multi_day_end_date":"Saturday, October 31, 2026","url":"https://nus.libcal.com/event/5972294","color":"#B3C8EF","locationCount":1,"location":"Exhibition Space, L1 (Art Gallery)","locations":[{"id":55590,"name":"Exhibition Space, L1 (Art Gallery)","map":"","mapId":0,"last":true}],"campus":"Central Library","presenter":"","featured_image":"","featured_image_alt_text":"","audiences":[{"id":1845,"name":"Anyone","color":"#2B9E08"}],"categories":"Exhibition","categories_arr":[{"cat_id":45666,"name":"Exhibition","color":"#B3C8EF"}],"calendar":"